          "english_quote": "Literal “many foods” preserves the concrete image of excess at table; a footnote clarifies the nuance of abundance/delicacies.",
          "issue": "The lexical rationale claims that a footnote clarifies abundance or delicacies, but no supplied footnote provides that clarification. This inaccurately describes the reader-facing documentation.",
          "suggested_revision": "Remove the claim that this clarification appears in a footnote, or supply a source-grounded lexical note distinguishing the selected rendering from the proposed alternatives. Any added note requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ῥήματα δικαιοσύνης",
          "english_quote": "Literal rendering retains the concrete focus on speech that accords with righteousness; footnote supplies an idiomatic alternative.",
          "issue": "No supplied footnote gives an idiomatic alternative to “words of righteousness.” The alternatives in lexical metadata are not a reader-facing footnote, so the rationale misreports what readers receive.",
          "suggested_revision": "Change the rationale to say that alternatives are recorded in lexical metadata, or add and review a reader-facing note giving a source-grounded alternative such as “righteous speech.”",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "simplified",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": false,
        "no_added_claims": true,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "Ἄκουε, φησί.",
          "english_quote": "He says, “Hold back from evil and do not do it.",
          "issue": "Paragraph 2 omits the shepherd’s explicit command “Listen.” The subsequent moral instruction is preserved, but this introductory directive is not represented.",
          "suggested_revision": "Proposed correction: “He says, ‘Listen. Hold back from evil and do not do it.’” Review the replacement in its full paragraph before acceptance.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἀπὸ ἐδεσμάτων πολλῶν",
          "english_quote": "Literal “many foods” preserves the concrete image of excess at table; a footnote clarifies the nuance of abundance/delicacies.",
          "issue": "The simplified edition independently contains the same inaccurate documentation claim: none of its supplied footnotes explains abundance or delicacies.",
          "suggested_revision": "Remove the unsupported statement about an existing footnote, or supply and freshly review a source-grounded lexical clarification appropriate to this edition.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ῥήματα δικαιοσύνης",
          "english_quote": "Literal rendering retains the concrete focus on speech that accords with righteousness; footnote supplies an idiomatic alternative.",
          "issue": "The simplified edition’s footnotes do not supply the claimed idiomatic alternative. Recording alternatives in copied lexical metadata does not fulfill this reader-facing documentation claim.",
          "suggested_revision": "Describe the alternatives as metadata rather than a footnote, or add and review an actual reader-facing lexical note.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Both editions were reviewed against the supplied Greek, with the simplified edition also compared independently with the standard. Apart from the findings above, the moral catalogs, practical services, good/evil contrast, necessity and negation, salvation assertion, and both ending conditions are represented faithfully. The selected working readings should remain: disclosed alternatives do not by themselves require replacement. The notes distinguish editorial supplementation and reported witness alternatives rather than presenting unanimous preserved Greek. Servant follows current policy, and the restoration instruction does not acquire an added repentance formula. This review does not verify unseen plates, editions, handwriting, or exhaustive collation. The revisions proposed here require fresh review and are not automatically accepted."
